{"repositoryId":1322177026,"availability":"available","full":"DevHusnainAi/zerodom","name":"zerodom","description":"Point an app at two logged-in users and it finds the broken access control (IDOR). Deterministic browser perception + cross-identity authz testing for AI agents — drives your real Chrome over MCP or runs headless. Open-core, local, no account.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-03T19:42:51Z","updated":"2026-10-17T12:51:56Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zerodom.vexralabs.com","topics":["ai-agents","appsec","attack-surface-mapping","authorization","broken-access-control","browser-automation","bug-bounty","claude","cli","computer-use","dom","idor","mcp","mcp-server","offensive-security","pentesting","playwright","security-tools","token-efficiency","zero-shot"],"demo":"https://zerodom.vexralabs.com/playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:02:07.621Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:02:07.621Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:02:07.621Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:02:07.621Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Point it at an app as two users. It finds the broken access control.","ZeroDOM drives your real, logged-in browser as two identities, replays the same requests as each, and flags where one user reaches what another can't — IDOR / broken access control, caught deterministically. Open-core, runs local, no account, no API key, nothing leaves your machine.","Under the hunt is a deterministic, token-lean perception engine for AI agents — the same core powers scan, crawl and any browser-driving task. IDOR is just where it bites hardest."],"features":["AppSec — compare / sweep: deterministic two-identity","AI agents — MCP: a flat interaction graph that cuts","access-boundary-split — one identity gets 200, the other 401/403 on an identical","cross-identity-identical-res